from lesson_data import P,S,E,Q,finish
LESSON=finish(dict(number=12,prereqs=[3,10,11],lead=P("Model catalogue records relationally, query them with SQL and preserve invariants with constraints and transactions.","用关系模型组织目录，通过 SQL 查询，借助约束与事务保持不变式。"),before=P("Know records and shared-state updates. SQLite is included with normal Python installations; the labs use temporary databases or memory.","了解记录与共享更新。通常 Python 包含 SQLite，实验使用临时库或内存。"),outcomes=[P("Design tables and keys.","设计表与键。"),P("Query and join with SQL.","用 SQL 查询与连接。"),P("Avoid duplicated facts.","避免重复事实。"),P("Explain index tradeoffs.","解释索引取舍。"),P("Use atomic transactions and parameterised values.","使用原子事务与参数化值。")],sections=[
S("Relations, keys and constraints","关系、键与约束","<p>A relational schema describes tables, columns and constraints. A primary key identifies a row; a foreign key refers to a key in another table. An author table plus book.author_id represents ownership without repeating the author's name everywhere. NOT NULL rejects missing required values, UNIQUE rejects duplicates and CHECK enforces local predicates. SQL tables are not ordered sequences: add ORDER BY when order matters. SQLite foreign-key enforcement must be enabled for each connection with PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON before relying on it.</p>","<p>关系模式描述表、列与约束。主键标识行，外键引用另一表键。作者表及 book.author_id 避免到处重复作者名。NOT NULL 拒绝必需值缺失，UNIQUE 拒绝重复，CHECK 约束局部谓词。表不是有序序列，需 ORDER BY。SQLite 每个连接需开启外键检查才能依赖它。</p>","Does SELECT without ORDER BY promise insertion order?","无 ORDER BY 的 SELECT 保证插入顺序吗？","No; specify ordering explicitly.","不保证，需明确排序。"),
S("Queries, joins and aggregation","查询、连接与聚合","<p>SELECT chooses columns, WHERE filters rows and JOIN combines rows satisfying a relationship. JOIN books to authors on author_id=id, not on coincidentally equal names. COUNT counts rows; GROUP BY forms groups before aggregation. NULL represents missing or unknown information, so use IS NULL rather than =NULL. A join can multiply rows when multiple matches exist: inspect key cardinalities before assuming one output per book. Parameter placeholders bind data values; they are not substitutes for arbitrary table or column names.</p>","<p>SELECT 选列，WHERE 筛行，JOIN 按关系组合。图书作者按 ID 连接，而非碰巧相同的名字。COUNT 计行，GROUP BY 聚合前分组。NULL 表示缺失或未知，应用 IS NULL。多匹配可使连接行数增加，需检查键基数。参数占位符绑定数据值，不能任意替代表或列名。</p>","Why join on author IDs rather than author names?","为何用作者 ID 而非名字连接？","Names need not be unique or stable.","名字未必唯一或稳定。"),
S("Normalisation and modelling","规范化与建模","<p>Repeated facts invite update anomalies: changing one author's name in many book rows can leave contradictory values. Store the author fact once and refer to it. A many-to-many book-author relationship needs a linking table with a composite key, not a comma-separated field. Model editions and physical copies separately if their identities differ. Normalisation helps consistency, but practical denormalisation may improve a measured workload if the update policy preserves correctness. Begin with the facts and dependencies, not the desired screen layout.</p>","<p>重复事实导致更新异常，多个图书行的作者名可能不一致。作者事实保存一次并引用。图书与作者多对多需带复合键连接表，而非逗号字段。版本与实体副本身份不同，应分别建模。规范化帮助一致性，实测需要时可反规范化，但更新策略须保持正确。先从事实与依赖出发。</p>","How should multiple authors per book be represented?","每本多作者如何表示？","A linking table of book_id and author_id pairs.","包含书 ID 与作者 ID 对的连接表。"),
S("Indexes and query plans","索引与查询计划","<p>An index is an additional lookup structure maintained alongside table data. It can reduce exact and range lookup work but consumes space and adds update cost. The database chooses a plan based on available structures and statistics; do not assume a declared index is used for every predicate. EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN shows the chosen access strategy. An index on title supports our exact title lookup; a leading-wildcard substring query may still scan. Measure the actual workload and include write costs before adding many indexes.</p>","<p>索引是随表维护的查询结构，能减少精确或范围查询工作，但占空间并增加更新成本。数据库根据结构与统计选择计划，不能假定每个谓词都用索引。EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN 显示策略。书名索引支持精确查询，前导通配子串可能仍扫描。增加索引前需测量负载并计写成本。</p>","Why not index every column automatically?","为何不自动索引每列？","Indexes cost storage and maintenance and may not help the workload.","索引占空间与维护成本，未必有用。"),
S("Transactions and safe queries","事务与安全查询","<p>A transaction groups changes so they commit together or roll back. Atomicity prevents a loan existing without its stock update; isolation controls interactions between concurrent transactions; durability concerns committed data surviving failures under the database's guarantees. Our conditional UPDATE decreases stock only when copies&gt;0, and the loan insert belongs to the same transaction. Bind user values with ? placeholders so input remains data instead of SQL syntax. Input validation and query parameterisation are complementary; neither replaces authorisation.</p>","<p>事务让修改一起提交或回滚。原子性避免借阅与库存不一致，隔离管理并发交互，持久性关注已提交数据在数据库保证下抗故障。条件 UPDATE 仅在库存正数时扣减，插入借阅属同一事务。用户值用 ? 绑定，保持为数据而非 SQL 语法。输入验证与参数化互补，都不能代替授权。</p>","If loan insertion fails after decrement, what must happen?","扣减后借阅插入失败应怎样？","Roll back the decrement as part of the same transaction.","作为同一事务回滚扣减。")],
labs=[dict(file="m12_database.py",title=P("Persist and query","持久保存与查询"),intro=P("Create an author/book schema, join it, inspect an index and reopen the file to verify persistence across connections.","建作者图书模式、连接、检查索引，重新打开文件确认跨连接保存。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Add another book for the same author.</li><li>Try an invalid author_id.</li><li>Run a grouped book count per author.</li></ol>","<ol><li>加入同作者另一图书。</li><li>尝试无效作者 ID。</li><li>按作者统计书数。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>Reuse author_id=1; invalid foreign IDs raise IntegrityError. GROUP BY author_id with COUNT(*) returns two after insertion. An outer join is needed to include authors with zero books.</p>","<p>复用作者 ID 一，无效外键抛 IntegrityError。插入后按作者分组 COUNT 为二，包含零书作者需外连接。</p>")),dict(file="m12_transactions.py",title=P("Atomic borrowing","原子借阅"),intro=P("A duplicate request fails after an attempted decrement, which must roll back. The lab rejects duplicates; Module 14 implements idempotent replay instead.","重复请求在尝试扣减后失败，扣减须回滚。本实验拒绝重复，模块 14 将实现幂等重放。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Remove transaction grouping and identify the broken invariant.</li><li>Test an unknown book.</li><li>Explain why a conditional UPDATE is better than an unprotected check followed by decrement.</li></ol>","<ol><li>移除事务分组，指出破坏不变式。</li><li>测试未知图书。</li><li>解释条件更新为何优于未保护先查再扣。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>Committing the decrement before a failed insert loses inventory without a loan. Unknown books affect zero rows and are rejected. Conditional mutation combines the availability predicate and update, avoiding a stale separate read.</p>","<p>插入失败前已提交扣减会无借阅地丢库存。未知书影响零行，拒绝。条件修改合并库存谓词与更新，避免单独陈旧读取。</p>"))],
exercises=[E(1,"Keys","键","Distinguish primary and foreign keys.","区分主外键。","<p>A primary key identifies a row; a foreign key references another candidate key and enforces the relationship when enabled.</p>","<p>主键标识行，外键引用其他候选键，并在启用时约束关系。</p>"),E(1,"Ordering","排序","How do you request books sorted by title then ID?","如何按书名再 ID 排序？","<p>SELECT id,title FROM books ORDER BY title,id.</p>","<p>使用 ORDER BY title,id。</p>"),E(2,"Missing values","缺失值","Why is title=NULL not the null check?","为何 title=NULL 不是空值检查？","<p>NULL participates in unknown-valued comparisons; use title IS NULL.</p>","<p>NULL 比较产生未知，应使用 IS NULL。</p>"),E(2,"Many-to-many","多对多","Design authorship for books with several authors.","设计多作者关系。","<p>book_authors(book_id,author_id) with a composite primary key and foreign keys to both entities.</p>","<p>使用两 ID 的连接表、复合主键与双方外键。</p>"),E(2,"Injection","注入","How should a quoted title be passed to SQL?","带引号书名如何传给 SQL？","<p>execute('SELECT id FROM books WHERE title=?',(title,)); do not interpolate it into the SQL text.</p>","<p>使用占位符与参数元组，不插入 SQL 文字。</p>"),E(3,"Invariant","不变式","State the borrowing stock invariant.","陈述借阅库存不变式。","<p>For each book, available copies plus active loans equals total copies, assuming no additions/returns during the operation. Changes must preserve it atomically.</p>","<p>无新增退还时，可用副本加有效借阅等于总副本，操作需原子保持。</p>"),E(3,"Failure recovery","失败恢复","A transaction decrements then violates UNIQUE. Final state?","事务扣减后违反唯一约束，最终状态？","<p>If the exception leaves the transaction context and triggers rollback, both changes are undone and the earlier committed state remains.</p>","<p>异常离开事务上下文触发回滚，双方修改撤销，保留此前提交状态。</p>"),E(2,"Index tradeoff","索引取舍","Why may adding a title index slow imports?","书名索引为何可能使导入变慢？","<p>Each insert must also maintain the index, adding work and storage writes.</p>","<p>每次插入还维护索引，增加工作与写入。</p>")],
quiz=[Q("A table has guaranteed output order?","表保证输出顺序吗？","Only with an explicit ordering request","需明确排序","Always insertion order","总插入顺序","Always primary-key order","总主键顺序","ORDER BY makes the requirement explicit.","ORDER BY 明确要求。"),Q("SQLite foreign keys should be?","SQLite 外键应怎样？","Enabled per connection","每连接启用","Ignored","忽略","Encoded as commas","编码为逗号","Enable before depending on enforcement.","依赖检查前启用。"),Q("A transaction failure should?","事务失败应怎样？","Rollback its grouped changes","回滚组合修改","Keep half the operation","保留一半","Delete every table","删所有表","Atomicity rules out partial application.","原子性排除部分应用。"),Q("Parameter placeholders protect?","参数占位符保护什么？","Data from becoming SQL syntax","数据不成为 SQL 语法","All authorisation","所有授权","Physical disk failure","物理磁盘故障","They are not a permission system.","它们不是权限系统。"),Q("An index costs?","索引有何成本？","Space and update maintenance","空间与更新维护","Nothing","无成本","Only a browser refresh","仅刷新浏览器","Lookup benefits have tradeoffs.","查询收益有取舍。"),Q("Unknown value check?","未知值检查？","IS NULL","IS NULL","=NULL","=NULL","==empty string always","总比较空字符串","NULL differs from empty text.","NULL 不同于空文字。")],pitfalls=[P("Connection context management handles transactions, not automatically connection closure.","连接上下文处理事务，不自动关闭连接。"),P("Uniqueness and indexes are related but not interchangeable requirements.","唯一性与索引相关，但要求不同。")],reading=[(P("SQLite transactions","SQLite 事务"),"https://www.sqlite.org/lang_transaction.html",P("Read commit/rollback and write transactions; describe a partial-update failure.","阅读提交回滚与写事务，描述部分更新失败。")),(P("Python sqlite3 tutorial","Python sqlite3 教程"),"https://docs.python.org/3/library/sqlite3.html",P("Read placeholders and connection management; explain closure versus rollback.","阅读占位符与连接管理，区分关闭与回滚。"))],terms=[(P("Primary key","主键"),P("A unique row identifier.","唯一行标识。")),(P("Transaction","事务"),P("A grouped operation with commit/rollback semantics.","具有提交回滚语义的组合操作。")),(P("Normalisation","规范化"),P("Organising facts around dependencies to reduce anomalies.","按依赖组织事实以减少异常。"))],review=P("<p>Draw the author/book schema and explain a failed loan transaction. Module 13 explores how programs themselves become structured input and where computation has limits.</p>","<p>画作者图书模式，解释失败借阅事务。模块 13 将把程序本身作为结构化输入，并探究计算边界。</p>")))
